Unreleased (PCB V2)
- Align each J2 label with its pin and identify the supply as 3V3.
- Enforce 0.3 mm copper-to-edge clearance, move the bottom ground bridge inward,
  and refill copper zones.
- Replace U1 with TI TLV1117LV33DCYR (C15578), retaining the 22u ceramic C2.
- Move U2 closer to USB, route both data lines across the ESD pads, keep the
  main pair together over ground, and add ground stitching by the crossover.
- Remove the RX/TX LEDs and their drivers (D1/D2, Q3/Q4, R3-R6), and move
  the remaining power LED and resistor beside J2's 3V3 pin with a PWR label.
- Replace Micro-USB with HRO TYPE-C-31-M-12 USB-C (C165948), keeping USB 2.0
  data and nominal 5 V input. Add separate 5.1k CC resistors R8/R9, move U2
  to fit the connector, and reroute the USB and connector power connections.
- Refresh schematic/board previews, manufacturing archives and BOMs.

v1.0.1
- No changes, remanufacturing in JLCPCB, updated P/N
- Updated kicad version

First release tag v1.0
- Initial release
- Tested and manufactured in JLCPCB
